  "body": [
    "South Ends begins a multi-term project addressing the vacant land once occupied by the refinery in South Philadelphia. It works from two directions: water quality and flood risk, and public access to a waterfront the city does not otherwise have. Letting the southernmost end return to nature provides protection against storm surge, while cutting a river through the site gives the control an urban waterfront needs under a changing climate.",
    "The inhabited areas are grouped into large neighborhoods, each with its own character and transit provision, linked by greenways and trolley lines that connect the site to the wider city. Where these organizing structures collide, the resulting fabric leaves room for less predictable design."
  ],
